{"name":"Fantasy Astronomy","title":"Fantasy Astronomy","revision":230869,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Fantasy_Astronomy","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fantasy Astronomy centers around the depiction of the study of astronomy and astrology in fictional fantasy settings. These visuals are based on astronomers during the Scientific Revolution (16th-17th centuries) but are included in stories with magic systems and feudal politics, with a setting, usually an observatory that has whimsical architecture and scholarly characters."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"The astronomy depicted in the fictional situations and aesthetic pictures is much simpler and magical than actual astronomy, as mapping constellations, making observations through a telescope, astrology, divination, and how the stars relate to the fictional world's magic system are common areas of study for the character or visual design."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fantasy Astronomy depicts imagery and research of the cosmos. Certain aspects of this aesthetic are similar to Academia aesthetics - with books of astronomy, telescopes, and star maps."},{"kind":"list","text":"Imagery of planets, moons, and stars."},{"kind":"list","text":"Telescopes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nighttime"},{"kind":"list","text":"Galaxy artwork"},{"kind":"list","text":"Astronomy textbooks and research papers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Magic-like depictions of astronomy"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Victorian era and Victorian-inspired fashion as well as fashion from around the 1920s-1960 is included in the typical style of dress for Fantasy Astronomy. You might also find some elements of uniforms for academias. The fashion style is often showcased by starry-themed Victorian or vintage clothing. Also note that the star/space/celestial motifs don’t need to be present on every outfit or object. Clothing is not gender specific, nor any style of makeup or hair is specified. which is one of the ways the fashion might deviate from the time eras it takes from."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Accessories"},{"kind":"list","text":"Messenger bags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nicer backpacks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather satchels or book bags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Newsboy caps"},{"kind":"list","text":"Student bags"},{"kind":"list","text":"Briefcases"},{"kind":"list","text":"Capes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cloaks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Headbands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Top hats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ties"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bows"},{"kind":"list","text":"Earrings"},{"kind":"list","text":"Suspenders"},{"kind":"list","text":"Necklaces"},{"kind":"list","text":"Glasses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Monocles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Watches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Socks of any length"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Tops"},{"kind":"list","text":"Collared shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sweaters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long sleeve and mid-sleeve shirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Blazers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pea coats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Oversized cardigans or sweaters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Blazers or jackets with elbow patches"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vests and waistcoats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pinafores"},{"kind":"list","text":"Blouses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Corset vests"},{"kind":"list","text":"Peter Pan collars"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Bottoms"},{"kind":"list","text":"Pleated skirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Victorian split skirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Trousers/Dress pants"},{"kind":"list","text":"Riding trousers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Non-ripped jeans"},{"kind":"list","text":"Formal Skorts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long skirts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Midi skirts"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Shoes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Boots (of any length)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Loafers"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mary Janes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Victorian-style shoes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kitten and short heels"},{"kind":"list","text":"Swing dance shoes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Lace up boots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Riding boots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Brogues"},{"kind":"list","text":"Combat boots"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Patterns and Prints"},{"kind":"list","text":"Plaid"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gingham"},{"kind":"list","text":"Galaxy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stars"},{"kind":"list","text":"Celestial"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vintage Celestial"},{"kind":"list","text":"Patents"},{"kind":"list","text":"Notes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hounds-tooth"},{"kind":"list","text":"Star glitter"},{"kind":"list","text":"Small accents of lace"},{"kind":"list","text":"Small amounts of holograph/iridescence"},{"kind":"list","text":"Patched or quilted details"},{"kind":"list","text":"Newspaper"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Activities"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Anything that involves astronomy can be considered an activity of Fantasy Astronomy."},{"kind":"list","text":"Stargazing"},{"kind":"list","text":"Studying astronomy"},{"kind":"list","text":"Using apps that use star maps"},{"kind":"list","text":"Painting starry nights, solar systems, and galaxies."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Books"},{"kind":"list","text":"Astronomy for Amateurs by Camille Flammarion (1904)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Zodiac Series by Rhomina Russell"},{"kind":"list","text":"Project Hail Mary by Andy Weir"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Film"},{"kind":"list","text":"A Trip to the Moon (1902)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Adventures of Baron Munchausen (1989)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Project Hail Mary (2026)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Starry Sky (2008)"},{"kind":"list","text":"No Man's Sky (2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Super Mario Galaxy (2007)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Characters"},{"kind":"list","text":"Urianger Augurelt from Final Fantasy XIV (2010)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Moonlight Cookie from Cookie Run: OvenBreak/Cookie Run: Kingdom (2016/2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Aaravos from The Dragon Prince (2018)"},{"kind":"list","text":"One from Battle for Dream Island: The Power of Two (2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stolas from Helluva Boss (2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mona Megistus and Layla from Genshin Impact (2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rosalina from Super Mario Galaxy (2007)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Xingchen (Stardust) from Vocaloid 4 and Synthesizer V Studio (2014/2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Various characters from Starry Sky"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sunday from Honkai: Star Rail (2023)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Astro from Dandy's World (2024)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Nightmini and Nightly from Anicats by The creator of Samo Login of Outfit7 (2009)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Starry and Navie from Anicats:Super Sweet Team (Sakura Studio 2013-2023)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Taro from Animeneko:Sweet of the Dreams S10 Dizzy Dreams (1999-2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Puffy Cottoncandy from Animeneko:Forever Super! (ア二メネコ:永遠に最高!)"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Resources"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Vendors"},{"kind":"list","text":"JuneSecrets"},{"kind":"list","text":"Daisydiytime"},{"kind":"list","text":"ETEREshop"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Music"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Songs"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Astronomy\" by Conan Gray (2021)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Moon Song\" by Phoebe Bridgers (2020)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"Galaxies\" by Laura Veirs (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"\"rises the moon\" by Liana Flores (2019)"}],"contentStatus":"full-source","images":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/cc/Wizardcore4.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20210121135610","caption":"Wizardcore4","source":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/File:Wizardcore4.jpg","remote":true,"local":"images/detail/0361-1.webp","localAvailable":true},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3